sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 035 Pass 2 Assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) & Scarpella et al. (2006) PIN1 efflux carrier allocation, intracellular pool conservation, and open dendritic trees vs closed reticulate venation loops — MorphoEval overall 93.0/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py` (overall weighted score: 93.1/100, up from 54.6/100 in v1). The remediated script integrates Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) hexagonal cell-level auxin S_i and 6-face PIN1 efflux carrier P_ij dynamics with exact intracellular pool conservation (P_{i,cyt} + sum_{j=1}^6 P_{ij} = P_total, error 0.0) and pairwise flux antisymmetry (J_{i->j} + J_{j->i} = 0, error 0.0); sweeps 6 allocation regimes across p in [0.8, 2.0] and saturating Hill exocytosis (Pearson r = 0.9999, p = 3.0e-8); demonstrates the topological transition on a 2D hexagonal leaf lamina lattice between Model A open dendritic trees (Betti-1 = 0 loops) and Model B + Scarpella et al. (2006) closed reticulate venation networks (Betti-1 = 16 loops bridged by 16 bipolar PIN1 cells, vs 0 loops under k_1 = 0 `gnom`/`pin1` ablation); and segments the SHA-256-locked cleared dicot leaf tip venation skeleton (`leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg`, Betti-1 = 205 closed areole loops, vein density 0.3585, mean areole compactness 0.7749 +- 0.0191 SE). Overall 93.0/100 (faithfulness 92.8, reproducibility 93.4); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/carrier_driven_canalization_comparison.png: rendered output of 2005-feugier-carrier-driven-canalization.py at 8871db0, image/png, 1258625 B, 2310×1428 px, artifact_sha256 60cbe1252bda975adf8955499006240bf329d5e1894f7dab81e6ae0ca89aa749 (sha256 60cbe1252bda975adf8955499006240bf329d5e1894f7dab81e6ae0ca89aa749), spec_fingerprint 2ca741f07ba825a876d0c45589ff7d455ac853c85ef60af0feb96546555dd50c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 2ca741f07ba825a876d0c45589ff7d455ac853c85ef60af0feb96546555dd50c; artifact_sha256: 60cbe1252bda975adf8955499006240bf329d5e1894f7dab81e6ae0ca89aa749; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/carrier_driven_canalization_reference.json=d1b984c1cb7883c5..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg=e54c8add6cf7c916..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/paper_citations.bib=cb81009f386f3a51..., datasets/carrier_driven_canalization/scout_manifest.json=1de2b4f4c53ac234...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-carrier-driven-canalization-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:313-325 hexagonal leaf lamina auxin S_i and directional PIN1 carrier P_ij ODEs with conserved total cellular carrier pool P_total = P_{i,cyt} + sum_{j=1}^6 P_ij, proving that conserved superlinear allocation Phi(J)=J^p (p > 1) forces winner-take-all single-face polarization and strictly open hierarchical dendritic venation trees (Betti-1 = 0), whereas nonlinear saturating allocation Phi(J)=J^n/(K^n+J^n) allows multi-face co-polarization and closed venation loops (Betti-1 > 0) | Scarpella, Marcos, Friml & Berleth (2006) Genes & Development 20:1015-1027 ProPIN1:PIN1-GFP imaging showing epidermal PIN1 convergence points and transient bipolar (double-headed) PIN1 cells bridging secondary strands into closed areole loops; reconstructed_in_script: 6-face hexagonal intracellular PIN1 pool conservation and regime bifurcation solver verifying exact pool conservation (error 0.0 < 1e-15), winner-take-all single-face polarization under Model A p=2.0 (dominant face share 0.9978 vs ref 0.9960), bipolar co-polarization under Model B saturating Hill exocytosis (dominant face share 0.5221 vs ref 0.5180), and 6-regime Pearson r = 0.9999 (p = 3.0e-8, RMSE = 0.0065) | 2D hexagonal leaf lamina lattice solver (14x14 ovate blade, 6 faces/cell) verifying pairwise intercellular auxin flux antisymmetry |J_{i->j} + J_{j->i}| = 0.0 and demonstrating the topological transition from Model A open dendritic venation trees (Betti-1 = 0 loops, 10 free vein endings, 0 bipolar bridge cells) to Model B + Scarpella epidermal convergence closed reticulate venation networks (Betti-1 = 16 loops, 16 bipolar PIN1 bridge cells), plus a k_1 = 0 (`gnom`/`pin1` exocytosis block) negative control (0 loops, 0.0 vein fraction) | Automated ridge + chromatic warmth segmentation of the cleared dicot leaf tip venation skeleton specimen (`leaf_tip_venation_loops_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0, 539x351 px) extracting vein density (0.3585), Betti-1 = 205 closed polygonal areole loops, mean areole area (99.06 px^2), and mean areole compactness (0.7749 +- 0.0191 SE); transfer_boundary: 2D hexagonal cellular leaf lamina lattice PIN1 carrier-flux dynamics and graph cycle-rank topology mapped to cleared dicot leaf venation skeleton; does_not_claim: 3D viscoelastic cell-wall mechanical expansion coupled to turgor-driven leaf blade growth." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 2D hexagonal PIN1 carrier-flux lattice to a growing biomechanical leaf blade mesh to simulate sequential emergence of primary, secondary, tertiary, and quaternary vein orders during blade expansion." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.93"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
}

